this is 28 year old Andrew banks from  Stansted in Essex he was attending that  protest in Parliament Square a protest  that was designed we're told to protect  statues and monuments around that  Parliament Square area but this young  man said that he had no idea what  monuments he was actually guarding and  that he was with a group of football  lads Alliance one of a number of groups  including right-wing groups who were at  this protest in Parliament Square he had  consumed 16 pints overnight and into  Saturday morning when he arrived in the  square apparently he said he was very  drunk his legal team told Westminster  magistrates court that he had no idea  what he was doing when he was  photographed urinating next to the  memorial of PC Keith Palmer that police  officer who was martyred outside  Parliament as he tried to protect the  houses of parliament from a terrorist  attacker in March of 2017 and of course  the images went into the press and on  social media gained a lot of traction  and resulted in a lot of revulsion as  well to bias elwood the Conservative MP  who had gone to try in vain to help PC  Keith Palmer on the day he was attacked  said that he found the images abhorrent  and in court today the senior magistrate  Emma Arbuthnot who sentenced this young  man to 14 days in jail said that she  accepted that he was drunk that he was  genuinely remorseful and didn't realize  what he was doing but that the was such  widespread revulsion of what he had done  that she had no choice but to jail him  for two weeks he's now being taken down  into custody and will serve as I say two  weeks in prison for that offence  it looks like he might have got off  quite lightly given that the government  wants to introduce 10 years possibly for  defiling monuments  well certainly I mean I think as far as  the charges concerned Emma Arbuthnot was  going off previous charges about  reaching public decency and it was felt  that a month reduces to two weeks  because he had come forward and admitted  to the offense when his father  confronted him after these images were  widely circulated he admitted it as I  see he claimed that he had no idea what  he was doing so mr bath Mort basing or  sentencing on previous similar cases  came up with this 14 days in custody but  you're right there are other people who  have still to go through the court  system and remember there are people  that have defaced statues and other  monuments as well who have still to face  court proceedings so it will be  interesting to find out what sentences  they get in the weeks ahead
 

